  "guidance": "The http connector allows users to issue http(s) requests.\n\n### Read\nGet data from a HTTP(S) endpoint.\n\n### Recipe\n```yaml\nread:\n  - http:\n      url: https://data.example.com\n      method: GET\n```\n\n### Function\n```python\nfrom wrangles.connectors import http\ndf = http.read(\n    url='https://data.example.com',\n    method='GET'\n)\n```\n\n### Write\nWrite data to a HTTP(S) endpoint.\n\n### Recipe\n```yaml\nread:\n  - http:\n      url: https://data.example.com\n      method: POST\n```\n\n### Function\n```python\nfrom wrangles.connectors import http\ndf = http.read(\n    url='https://data.example.com',\n    method='POST'\n)\n```"
